1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,000
Marie Curie's notebooks are still

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,780
radioactive. In 1898, she and Pierre found

3
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:09,440
two new elements, polonium, then radium.

4
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:12,580
Radium glowed in the dark, and she handled

5
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:14,740
it for years with no protection.

6
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:18,320
Today, her papers sit in lead-lined boxes

7
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:22,900
in Paris. Radium takes 1,600 years to lose

8
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:23,880
half its strength
